      "message": "Yes, b/199259751 is to determine the \"client\"\u0027s CID.  But aren\u0027t you trying to return the \"server\"\u0027s CID to the client?\n\nSince the client should already have an IVirtualMachine instance, I think you can just call IVirtualMachine.getCid()?  Then you could avoid the workaround and simply pass a dummy value of CID back (until the argument is removed).",
